    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0065" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/4–946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent   niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-09T18:00:00+01:00">April 9, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 9—1:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1692. For the Secretary. Following is translation of a second note (my 1649,
                    April 7)<anchor n="69" xml:id="d38-f1"/> delivered at same time as French reply
                    on meeting of Council of Foreign Ministers transmitted in my immediately
                    preceding telegram: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Mr. Ambassador: I have informed Your Excellency that the French Govt
                            accepted the proposal of the Secretary of State regarding the meeting of
                            the Council of Foreign Ministers on April 25 at Paris.</p>
                        <p>The French Govt trusts (compte) that this meeting of the Council of
                            Foreign Ministers will be the occasion to examine German questions to
                            which the French Govt had already drawn attention of the United States
                            Govt by its communication of the first of March last reaffirming the
                            terms of its memorandum of September 13.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d38-f2"
                            /></p>
                        <p>Please accept, Mr. Ambassador, et cetera. Signed:
                    Bidault.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d38-f1" n="69" xml:id="d38-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d38-f2" n="70" xml:id="d38-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to the memorandum by the French Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                    Ministers, entitled “Control and Administration of Germany” and designated
                        C.F.M. (45) 17, September 13, 1945, <ref
                        target="frus1945v02#pg_177"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1945, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 177</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
